  "annotation_notes": {
    "workflow_logic": "This workflow performs FASTQ quality control, trimming, filtering and strandedness detection. Key features: (1) Concatenates FASTQ files from same sample, (2) Performs linting checks at multiple stages, (3) Supports two trimming alternatives: TrimGalore or fastp, (4) Optionally removes genome contaminants with BBSplit, (5) Optionally removes rRNA with SortMeRNA, (6) Infers strandedness using Salmon pseudoalignment",
    "conditional_paths": "Two main execution paths based on trimmer parameter: TrimGalore path (steps 10,12,14,16,19,21,23) or fastp path (steps 11,13,15,17,20,22,24). BBSplit and SortMeRNA steps are optional based on skip_bbsplit and remove_ribo_rna parameters.",
    "data_flow": "Reads flow through concatenation \u2192 linting \u2192 trimming (alternative paths) \u2192 post-trim linting \u2192 BBSplit filtering \u2192 post-BBSplit linting \u2192 SortMeRNA filtering \u2192 post-SortMeRNA linting \u2192 Salmon strandedness inference"
  }
